cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use COMET in your research, please cite the preprint below."
title: "COMET: Cost-function Optimized Maximal Overlap Drift EsTimation"
abstract: >-
  COMET is a fast, GPU-accelerated software package for drift correction in
  single-molecule localization microscopy (SMLM) datasets. It achieves high
  spatial and temporal resolution by maximizing spatiotemporal overlap across
  frames using a cost-function optimization approach.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/gpufit/Comet"
url: "https://comet.smlm.tools/"
version: 1.1.0
keywords:
  - single-molecule localization microscopy
  - super-resolution microscopy
  - drift correction
  - STORM
  - MINFLUX
  - GPU
